From c11c76fc9f8a0bbf97c4145ef62a7a949765ff37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:10:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Security hardening: fix auth bypass, CSRF/DNS rebinding,
 SSRF, path traversal

Critical
- Auth bypass: the auth hook tested the raw URL for "/api/", but the router
  decodes %-escapes, so "/%61pi/settings" (or "/a%70i/fs/dirs?path=/etc")
  reached the API without a login. The hook now decides by the matched
  route (and the decoded path).

High
- CSRF / cross-site WebSocket: state-changing API calls and /api/ws are
  refused when Origin or Sec-Fetch-Site says another site sent them. This
  mattered most while the local machine is trusted without a login.
- DNS rebinding: "local machine" trust now also requires a local Host
  header (IP, localhost, or this machine's name).
- Path traversal: torrents whose file paths escape the save folder
  (backslash "..", absolute, drive or ADS paths) are refused when added
  and when magnet metadata arrives (parse-torrent only resolves "/" parts).
- SSRF: links from feed items and search results may only reach public
  addresses unless they point at the feed's / Torznab endpoint's own host;
  redirects are followed manually and checked per hop.
- First-run takeover: creating the first login from another device needs
  a one-time setup code printed in the server log.

Medium / low
- Changing the login needs the current password; removing it is local-only.
- Login always runs the password hash (no username timing oracle).
- API tokens (?token=, apikey, passkey) are redacted from request logs.
- Electron: exact-origin navigation check (prefix test let other local
  ports in), IPC only from our UI, openPath never executes files.
- WebSocket maxPayload 64 KiB; watch-folder files capped at 16 MiB;
  release titles capped before regex parsing; failure table bounded.
- Config dir 0700, database 0600 (it holds passkey feed URLs).
- Headers: CORP/COOP same-origin, Permissions-Policy, CSP connect-src 'self';
  Secure cookie behind TLS proxies.
- CI token limited to contents:read; runtime image applies Debian updates.
- Redacted a tracker passkey committed in feeds.json and
  download_rules.json (it remains in git history: rotate it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013nmSf2zmYoNEfzcNutPGUX
